WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:52.400
[Music]

00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:56.800
[Narrator: The United States Public Health Service as it exists today is the product of experience

00:00:56.809 --> 00:01:00.199
extending over a period of nearly 150 years.

00:01:00.199 --> 00:01:04.860
It was originally created as a Marine Hospital
service for the purpose of providing medical

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:07.300
care to American merchant seaman.

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:11.600
The Marine Hospital service was established
by an Act of Congress signed by the second

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:16.720
president of the United States, John Adams,
on July 16, 1798.

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:26.420
This service was originally supported by a
tax on American merchant seaman, but this

00:01:26.430 --> 00:01:28.189
tax was later abolished.

00:01:28.189 --> 00:01:32.390
The tax was collected by the collector of
customs of the Treasury Department, and the

00:01:32.390 --> 00:01:36.960
Marine Hospital Service came under the jurisdiction
of that department where it remains today.

00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:44.840
The first Marine Hospital, located at Norfolk,
Virginia, was purchased from that state in 1881.

00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:49.340
The second was built in Boston, Massachusetts
(unintelligible)

00:01:49.359 --> 00:01:54.090
and some of the medical personnel were utilized
by both the Union and the Confederacy for

00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:56.100
the care of the (unintelligible) wounded of
the military forces.

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:07.200
It frequently happened that the medical officers
of the early Marine Hospitals were the first

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:11.940
physicians to diagnose such diseases as cholera,
yellow fever, and smallpox, which seriously

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:14.030
endangered the public health at ports of entry.

00:02:14.030 --> 00:02:18.750
As time went on, the work of the Service became
of such increasing importance to the public

00:02:18.750 --> 00:02:23.770
health of the country that Congress gradually
extended its duties until it became in function

00:02:23.770 --> 00:02:25.160
a federal health service.

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:30.240
Recognizing the value of mobility and military
discipline in an organization which had to

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:32.250
combat epidemic diseases,

00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:36.890
Congress authorized the organization of the
Marine Hospital Service along military lines,

00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:41.140
with officers holding commissions and grades
similar to those of officers of the Medical

00:02:41.140 --> 00:02:42.300
Departments of the Army and the Navy.

00:02:42.700 --> 00:02:47.140
In 1912 the name of the Service was changed
to that borne by this organization today,

00:02:47.140 --> 00:02:49.380
the United States Public Health Service.

00:02:50.410 --> 00:02:54.700
The Public Health Service is administered
by the Surgeon General, who is responsible

00:02:54.700 --> 00:03:03.280
directly to the Secretary of the Treasury,
to Congress, and to the President of the United States.

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:08.440
We will now hear the Surgeon General briefly
outline the work of the Public Health Service.

00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:15.100
Although the first responsibility for public
health rests upon the states and localities

00:03:15.100 --> 00:03:20.460
in our country, the federal government, through
the Public Health Service, does much to prevent

00:03:20.460 --> 00:03:23.240
disease and improve the health of all the
people.

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:25.740
This is done in many ways.

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:31.960
One very skilled group of men and women (unintelligible)
of disease and means of preventing it.

00:03:33.620 --> 00:03:39.460
Other Service officers guard the ports to
prevent the introduction of disease from abroad.

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:46.800
Others have the duty of preventing and halting
the spread of infections within our own territory.

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:52.860
Under the provisions of the recently enacted
Social Security Act, the Public Health Service

00:03:52.870 --> 00:03:58.820
is cooperating with every state and territory
in the development, in those states and territories,

00:03:58.820 --> 00:04:00.840
of a national health program.

00:04:01.480 --> 00:04:06.140
This cooperative work between the federal,
state, and local governments should provide

00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:08.560
new standards of health for the people.

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:14.740
In addition, the manufacture of all serums
and vaccines sold in the country is carefully

00:04:14.740 --> 00:04:17.190
supervised by the Public Health Service.

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:22.940
Studies are carried out concerning drug addiction
and mental hygiene.

00:04:24.580 --> 00:04:29.320
It conducts Marine Hospitals in which are
treated American sailors.

00:04:30.380 --> 00:04:35.420
In addition, this Service keeps in constant
touch with health conditions throughout the

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:38.340
world, through weekly reports from every consular
officer.

00:04:39.220 --> 00:04:43.720
It encourages health education in various
problems of disease prevention.

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:53.300
In what follows, you will see, in much more
detail, the ways in which this organization operates for human service.

00:04:53.300 --> 00:05:06.780
[Music]

00:05:07.820 --> 00:05:12.280
For centuries it has been well known that
epidemic diseases follow the lines of commerce and travel.

00:05:13.740 --> 00:05:17.460
During colonial times and in the early days
of our republic, the introduction of yellow

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:23.460
fever, smallpox, cholera, and other diseases
from foreign countries by ship was by no means uncommon

00:05:24.160 --> 00:05:28.600
Epidemics of yellow fever from this source
occurred as late as 1798 in New York, in Baltimore

00:05:28.600 --> 00:05:32.440
as late as 1832, and in Philadelphia as late
as 1853.

00:05:33.560 --> 00:05:37.440
Many outbreaks of smallpox and cholera were
the result of cases brought in by vessels.

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:44.870
The danger of introduction of diseases from
abroad has paralleled in growth the remarkable

00:05:44.870 --> 00:05:46.960
development of transportation on the sea,

00:05:48.620 --> 00:05:49.280
on the land,

00:05:51.980 --> 00:05:53.220
and in the air.

00:05:56.050 --> 00:06:00.660
The transportation of disease has been as
much facilitated by improved mechanical methods

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:03.220
as has the transportation of persons or property.

00:06:06.600 --> 00:06:11.560
Maritime quarantine was at first undertaken
by the states and cities, but is now administered

00:06:11.560 --> 00:06:16.260
by the Public Health Service at all the ports
of the United States and its possessions.

00:06:17.280 --> 00:06:21.210
To perform these functions, the Service has
been given quarantine jurisdiction over all

00:06:21.210 --> 00:06:26.140
ships and all persons, both citizens and aliens,
coming into American ports from abroad.

00:06:26.820 --> 00:06:30.620
In its quarantine work, the United States
Public Health Service maintains a fleet of

00:06:30.620 --> 00:06:34.681
trim and speedy boarding tugs, which carry
the quarantine officers out to the vessels

00:06:34.681 --> 00:06:36.420
arriving at United States ports.

00:06:41.460 --> 00:06:46.660
When a vessel arrives at quarantine, the medical
quarantine officer, a nurse, and an inspector

00:06:46.660 --> 00:06:51.280
go out to it in one of these boarding tugs
so well known to seaman and ocean travelers.

00:06:56.120 --> 00:06:59.340
They draw alongside the vessel and go aboard.

00:07:04.360 --> 00:07:07.220
The quarantine officer meets the ship’s
doctor and the purser.

00:07:12.940 --> 00:07:17.360
The purser turns over to him certain records of the vessel's voyage for inspection,

00:07:17.360 --> 00:07:22.170
especially the bill of health and health record en route, which shows all cases of illness occurring

00:07:22.170 --> 00:07:23.360
on board during the trip.

00:07:29.840 --> 00:07:33.840
Ah, the list here shows a suspicious case
of illness in a member of the crew.

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:35.680
Let’s see now what happens.

00:07:41.200 --> 00:07:45.140
The quarantine officer is taken to the sick
bay in the crew's quarters to examine the patient.

00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:54.000
His experience and training in the detection
of the symptoms of rare as well as common diseases,

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:57.040
tells him that this patient is suffering
from typhus fever.

00:07:59.540 --> 00:08:01.860
He orders the patient to be removed from the
vessel,

00:08:09.620 --> 00:08:12.620
and put aboard the quarantine tug to be taken
ashore.

00:08:16.280 --> 00:08:20.360
All persons who have been in contact with
the patient, and thus have been exposed

00:08:20.360 --> 00:08:23.260
to the disease, are also ordered on board the tug.

00:08:26.920 --> 00:08:31.860
The patient and the contacts are taken to
the detention hospital, in this instance,

00:08:31.860 --> 00:08:33.500
Hoffman Island in New York Harbor.

00:08:41.140 --> 00:08:45.000
On their arrival, the sick patient is taken
directly to the hospital.

00:08:50.160 --> 00:08:54.160
Here he is given appropriate treatments and
cared for until he has recovered.

00:08:56.140 --> 00:09:01.320
Every facility is made available in such cases,
both for the benefit of the patient himself,

00:09:01.340 --> 00:09:02.480
and for the protection of others.

00:09:04.560 --> 00:09:09.000
As this happens to be a case of Old World
typhus fever, which is known to be spread

00:09:09.009 --> 00:09:13.709
by the body louse, the contacts, those who
have had association with the patient

00:09:13.709 --> 00:09:16.720
during the voyage, are first taken to the delousing plant.

00:09:19.960 --> 00:09:22.040
Here they must remove all of their clothing,

00:09:26.140 --> 00:09:27.660
Thoroughly sprayed with soap and water.

00:09:31.240 --> 00:09:32.680
Next they are sent under the shower.

00:09:37.160 --> 00:09:41.460
And finally, each one is sprayed with an insecticide
that kills any lice or nits that may still

00:09:41.460 --> 00:09:42.520
remain in their hair.

00:09:47.720 --> 00:09:52.240
The clothing of these contacts is placed in
net bags, and these bags are sent to the fumigating room.

00:09:53.320 --> 00:09:57.500
This clothing, together with the baggage of
the contacts, is placed in fumigating chambers

00:09:57.520 --> 00:09:59.360
where it is thoroughly disinfested.

00:10:00.300 --> 00:10:04.660
If necessary, the contacts are isolated in
the detention hospital for observation.

00:10:05.080 --> 00:10:09.720
Every precaution is taken by the quarantine
officers to prevent the introduction of disease

00:10:09.720 --> 00:10:10.880
into the United States.

00:10:13.620 --> 00:10:18.200
When the quarantine work has been completed,
and the ship declared free from danger, the

00:10:18.200 --> 00:10:21.520
medical officers of the Public Health Service
then turn to the inspection of immigrants.

00:10:25.440 --> 00:10:29.100
This scene shows the well-known immigration
station at Ellis Island New York.

00:10:33.960 --> 00:10:37.500
During the busy period of a few years ago,
more prospective citizens of this country

00:10:37.500 --> 00:10:41.899
arriving from abroad entered through this
world-renowned station than through any other

00:10:41.900 --> 00:10:42.840
port of the country.

00:10:43.140 --> 00:10:47.580
In past years thousands of aliens arrived
at Ellis Island daily, and each one had to

00:10:47.580 --> 00:10:51.700
undergo an examination at the hands of the
medical officers of the Public Health Service.

00:10:55.180 --> 00:10:59.640
In past times too, many of them arrived only
to be turned back at our very gate, because

00:10:59.640 --> 00:11:01.350
of mental or physical defects.

00:11:01.350 --> 00:11:07.230
This was a necessary, but somewhat cruel procedure,
and caused many heart aches, untold hardships,

00:11:07.230 --> 00:11:08.800
and much unnecessary expense.

00:11:09.600 --> 00:11:14.540
To avoid this condition, a new system was
inaugurated by international consent in 1925,

00:11:14.540 --> 00:11:19.029
since which year, intending immigrants have
been examined in foreign countries by Public

00:11:19.029 --> 00:11:23.360
Health Service officers who are assigned to
American consulates for this purpose.

00:11:23.360 --> 00:11:27.990
The prospective immigrant makes application
through the American consul, who, if the applicant

00:11:27.990 --> 00:11:32.000
comes within the quota prescribed by Congress,
arranges for an examination by the Public

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:33.160
Health Service medical officer.

00:11:33.780 --> 00:11:36.399
If the applicant passes these physical and
mental tests successfully, there is little

00:11:36.399 --> 00:11:37.399
chance that he will be refused admittance
later.

00:11:37.399 --> 00:11:38.399
[Historians have recorded that the Bubonic
Plague or the "Black Death" almost depopulated

00:11:38.400 --> 00:11:39.360
Europe during the Middle Ages.]

00:11:46.580 --> 00:11:57.040
[Webster on pestilence] Among other old records,
Webster's book on pestilence gives vivid descriptions

00:11:57.040 --> 00:11:58.900
of the many ravages of bubonic plague.

00:12:02.720 --> 00:12:39.800
[Panning shots of book pages]

00:12:39.980 --> 00:12:44.480
This disease is constantly present in the
Orient, and this fact makes it an ever present

00:12:44.480 --> 00:12:46.580
threat to the United States and its possessions.

00:12:50.120 --> 00:12:55.350
The germ that causes bubonic plague is carried
by fleas that live on rats and other rodents.

00:12:55.350 --> 00:13:00.600
Rats are great travelers, and vessels at wharves
must use rat guards to keep them from  coming aboard.

00:13:01.900 --> 00:13:04.120
Notice how this rat balances himself with
his tail.

00:13:04.660 --> 00:13:06.300
Now he attempts to clear the rat guard.

00:13:08.280 --> 00:13:09.140
Will he succeed?

00:13:10.560 --> 00:13:11.600
It looks like he'll make it.

00:13:13.940 --> 00:13:17.540
No, he admits defeat and he returns to the
wharf.

00:13:20.080 --> 00:13:24.900
Yellow fever, the fearful Yellow Jack which
once struck terror to the South, is one of

00:13:24.900 --> 00:13:28.480
the best examples of a dread disease now almost
entirely wiped out by science.

00:13:29.100 --> 00:13:31.860
It is transmitted principally by a particular
kind of mosquito.

00:13:32.300 --> 00:13:36.800
With the mosquitoes that transmit the disease
exterminated, yellow fever is eliminated.

00:13:40.080 --> 00:13:46.220
Although yellow fever has been banished from
our shores since 1905, it still exists in

00:13:46.220 --> 00:13:47.500
South America and Africa.

00:13:48.080 --> 00:13:51.940
And recent development in air travel again
make it a menace to the United States.

00:13:52.700 --> 00:13:57.799
To combat this menace, the yellow fever mosquito
must be eliminated from ships and airplanes,

00:13:57.800 --> 00:14:00.260
and infected persons must be detected and
isolated.

00:14:02.120 --> 00:14:06.560
Although the mosquitoes which spread yellow
fever usually fly but a relatively short distance,

00:14:06.980 --> 00:14:09.660
they have been carried by airplanes for thousands
of miles.

00:14:11.260 --> 00:14:16.739
It's only by the exercise of the utmost care
and constant watchfulness that this dangerous,

00:14:16.740 --> 00:14:18.940
ever-threatening disease is kept outside our
borders.

00:14:19.540 --> 00:14:24.339
When there arrives at a port of entry an airplane
which might bring in the yellow fever mosquito,

00:14:24.340 --> 00:14:27.560
the passengers and crew are inspected for
symptoms of the disease.

00:14:32.520 --> 00:14:36.120
An important part of the inspection is the
taking of the temperature for evidence of fever.

00:14:40.140 --> 00:14:44.140
The plane is gone over thoroughly with a vacuum
cleaner to recover any yellow fever mosquitoes

00:14:44.140 --> 00:14:45.200
that might be aboard.

00:14:49.720 --> 00:14:53.540
Then the cabin and all enclosed spaces in
the plane are sprayed with insecticide that

00:14:53.540 --> 00:14:55.160
destroy these dangerous pests.

00:14:57.100 --> 00:15:01.060
The opening of air routes to the Orient has
created serious problems in preventing the

00:15:01.080 --> 00:15:06.460
introduction of diseases, particularly cholera
and smallpox, into Hawaii and the United States.

00:15:09.120 --> 00:15:33.860
[Music]

00:15:34.440 --> 00:15:39.299
When the country was small, travel was slow
and distances in travelled time were much

00:15:39.299 --> 00:15:40.629
greater than they are today.

00:15:40.629 --> 00:15:44.860
Then there was less need for action on the
part of the federal government itself in preventing

00:15:44.860 --> 00:15:45.820
the spread of epidemics.

00:15:48.140 --> 00:15:52.540
But with the increased proclivity of travel,
the expansion in territories,

00:15:53.220 --> 00:15:57.440
and the concentration of populations, this
work became important.

00:16:03.980 --> 00:16:09.080
With increase in interstate traffic, the need
for uniform quarantine regulations became apparent.

00:16:09.500 --> 00:16:13.380
And by the consent of the states, and under
the commerce clause of the Constitution,

00:16:13.600 --> 00:16:17.440
Congress provided for federal control of both interstate
and international quarantine.

00:16:18.949 --> 00:16:23.200
The sanitary control over all water supplies
used for drinking or culinary purposes on

00:16:23.209 --> 00:16:27.540
interstate carriers is one of the activities
of the Public Health Service in connection

00:16:27.540 --> 00:16:29.819
with the prevention of the interstate spread
of disease.

00:16:30.140 --> 00:16:33.200
It is obvious that this is a tremendous task.

00:16:33.200 --> 00:16:36.560
The water included in these supplies comes
from almost 3,000 sources.

00:16:36.980 --> 00:16:41.551
In this work, the cooperation of state and
city health authorities is given to the Public

00:16:41.560 --> 00:16:42.120
Health Service.

00:16:43.520 --> 00:16:47.999
In taking supplies of drinking and culinary
water onboard vessels, connections are made

00:16:48.000 --> 00:16:49.280
directly to the supply pipes.

00:16:49.860 --> 00:16:54.160
And the possibility of contamination of the
water during this process is thereby reduced to a minimum.

00:16:55.120 --> 00:16:59.220
Here we see a supply of drinking water being
taken aboard a steamship at one of our ports.

00:17:02.980 --> 00:17:07.880
The same sanitary precautions are carried
out when drinking water is taken aboard trains.

00:17:07.880 --> 00:17:09.640
Frequent inspections are made of this procedure.

00:17:15.220 --> 00:17:19.040
The passenger can therefore feel a sense of
security when he quenches his thirst from

00:17:19.040 --> 00:17:20.100
the water cooler,

00:17:22.260 --> 00:17:25.260
or drinks water with his meals in the dining
car.

00:17:28.380 --> 00:17:31.240
The fight against bubonic plague is a fight
against the rat.

00:17:31.560 --> 00:17:37.480
He must be trapped, poisoned, starved out,
built out - everything must be done to rout this animal.

00:17:39.040 --> 00:17:42.580
The rat has been called man’s most destructive
and dangerous enemy.

00:17:42.580 --> 00:17:46.260
He is certainly a most dangerous pest in the
case of bubonic plague.

00:17:46.680 --> 00:17:51.600
He is sturdy, furtive, and crafty, and he
readily matches his cunning against that of to a minimum.

00:17:52.280 --> 00:17:56.740
The rat catcher must know the habits of this
animal, and it is only with such knowledge,

00:17:56.740 --> 00:17:58.240
combined with actual experience,

00:17:58.240 --> 00:18:02.540
that he can qualify as an expert in what may
indeed be called a specialized field.

00:18:08.180 --> 00:18:12.760
The rats are tagged to show the locality in
which they are caught, and are then sent to

00:18:12.760 --> 00:18:14.360
the laboratory for examination.

00:18:18.560 --> 00:18:22.800
Some of the rats that are taken alive are
put into bags to preserve for identification

00:18:22.800 --> 00:18:25.340
and examination of any fleas that they may
harbor.

00:18:30.060 --> 00:18:33.400
Here we see a sample day's catch of rats in
one of our large cities.

00:18:39.100 --> 00:18:44.040
At the laboratory, the rats are combed for
fleas, and their fleas are collected for study

00:18:44.049 --> 00:18:47.940
and for testing to determine whether or not
they are infected with bubonic plague.

00:19:03.820 --> 00:19:07.880
In certain western states, plague has spread
from rats to ground squirrels, and the fight

00:19:07.880 --> 00:19:10.660
against these animals is being constantly
carried on there.

00:19:17.980 --> 00:19:25.980
[Music]

00:19:27.800 --> 00:19:31.680
The following are typical scenes of the regions
in the east central sections of this country

00:19:31.680 --> 00:19:33.100
in which trachoma is chiefly found.

00:19:33.720 --> 00:19:37.700
In these rural sections, life was somewhat
primitive, and the sanitary conditions were

00:19:37.860 --> 00:19:42.480
conducive to the spread of the disease because
of the habits and customs of the people.

00:19:42.490 --> 00:19:47.250
They did not know that trachoma was spread
by means of the hands, and by towels and handkerchiefs,

00:19:47.250 --> 00:19:49.680
and other articles which may carry the discharges
from the eyes.

00:19:50.360 --> 00:19:56.720
Simply described, trachoma is a chronic infectious
disease of the lining membrane of the eyelid.

00:19:56.720 --> 00:20:01.840
If the lids are turned back, a number of small
granular bodies resembling Sago grains will

00:20:01.840 --> 00:20:02.840
be noticed.

00:20:02.840 --> 00:20:07.039
The disease produces a roughened condition
of the inside of the lid which irritates the

00:20:07.040 --> 00:20:12.040
front of the eyeball, causing an inflammation
which often leads to blindness.

00:20:16.740 --> 00:20:21.160
For many years, the Public Health Service
has conducted a campaign against this ancient disease.

00:20:21.940 --> 00:20:27.400
As early as 1912, Dr. John McMullen of the
Public Health Service was sent to Kentucky

00:20:27.400 --> 00:20:29.380
to make a survey of the situation there.

00:20:30.780 --> 00:20:34.020
"Dr. McMullen, what was found in Kentucky
and what was done there?"

00:20:35.720 --> 00:20:43.500
"Well, more than 18,000 persons were examined
in 1912, and between 7 and 8 percent were found to have trachoma.

00:20:44.500 --> 00:20:47.060
Many had already been blinded by the disease.

00:20:47.520 --> 00:20:51.120
Many others remained in dark rooms concealing
their eyes with their arms.

00:20:51.920 --> 00:20:56.120
Some had not seen light for months, while
many cases had existed for years.

00:20:58.420 --> 00:21:02.140
In checking up some years later, the changes
were remarkable.

00:21:03.240 --> 00:21:08.840
Instead of many sore-eyed people, and the
almost universal practice of wearing colored

00:21:08.840 --> 00:21:13.720
glasses observed during the first survey,
scarcely colored glass was seen,

00:21:13.880 --> 00:21:16.060
and few cases of active trachoma.

00:21:17.020 --> 00:21:21.740
From the standpoint of humane and economic
considerations, there is no way to estimate

00:21:21.880 --> 00:21:23.640
what this trachoma work has been worth.

00:21:25.060 --> 00:21:30.200
Much of the work was done in mountain regions,
where roads even now are not good.

00:21:30.800 --> 00:21:34.560
Usually medical officers traveled by horseback,
and often they had to walk.

00:21:36.160 --> 00:21:37.980
The work has now been turned over to the States."

00:21:40.460 --> 00:21:44.740
Instead of painful and sightless eyes to destroy
the joys of youth, we now have the precious

00:21:44.740 --> 00:21:45.850
gift of sight.

00:21:45.850 --> 00:21:48.740
The future must be dreary to one destined
to live in darkness.

00:21:48.740 --> 00:21:51.350
Fortunately this boy was discovered in time.

00:21:51.350 --> 00:21:55.840
Instead of blindness added to other infirmities
of old age, we have the ability to assume

00:21:55.840 --> 00:21:58.160
an economic role in family affairs.

00:22:05.560 --> 00:22:10.120
Numerous outbreaks of typhoid fever have followed
the use of shellfish grown in contaminated waters.

00:22:10.780 --> 00:22:15.740
This was a danger that could be combated
by examination of the waters where oysters were grown

00:22:15.800 --> 00:22:19.780
and forbidding the interstate shipment of
oysters originating in areas, the sanitary

00:22:19.789 --> 00:22:22.680
conditions of which, were not approved by
the Public Health Service.

00:22:24.260 --> 00:22:29.320
Because oysters from beds in contaminated
waters will not be certified, and shucking

00:22:29.330 --> 00:22:33.409
plants and canneries are required to be conducted
under proper sanitary conditions,

00:22:33.409 --> 00:22:36.860
the consumer can now enjoy this seafood with
a greater sense of security than formerly.

00:22:37.960 --> 00:22:49.940
[Music]

00:22:51.220 --> 00:22:55.420
An act of Congress authorizes an annual conference
between the Surgeon General and the state

00:22:55.420 --> 00:22:57.960
health officers to discuss important health
matters.

00:22:58.660 --> 00:23:01.040
Here the Surgeon General opens a recent conference.

00:23:03.340 --> 00:23:10.220
"This annual conference of state and territorial
health officers will come to order.

00:23:14.980 --> 00:23:17.000
I am delighted to greet you here today.

00:23:18.120 --> 00:23:23.680
One of the most significant events in public
health which has occurred in our lifetime

00:23:24.220 --> 00:23:32.540
transpired last month, when President Roosevelt
signed a bill appropriating funds to launch the health security program.

00:23:33.180 --> 00:23:39.000
This bill and the funds authorized under it
offer a great promise to the people of this

00:23:39.000 --> 00:23:40.240
country for better health.

00:23:40.880 --> 00:23:47.460
It is your task and my task to see that this
promise becomes a realization.

00:23:47.860 --> 00:23:54.580
It is to discuss the detailed means by which
we may obtain the objectives held forth in

00:23:54.580 --> 00:23:58.080
the Social Security Act that this conference
will be concerned.

00:23:58.680 --> 00:23:59.840
I welcome your advice.

00:24:00.840 --> 00:24:04.880
These conferences provide opportunities for
planning effective methods for state and federal

00:24:04.889 --> 00:24:07.980
cooperation in attacking health problems of
mutual concern.

00:24:08.480 --> 00:24:12.660
For many years, the Public Health Service
has cooperated with the state health officers

00:24:12.660 --> 00:24:15.680
in an effort to develop and improve state
and local health work.

00:24:16.140 --> 00:24:20.860
When necessary, experienced Service officers
are assigned as shown here, for periods of

00:24:20.860 --> 00:24:24.700
time to aid state and local health departments
in their special health problems.

00:24:25.400 --> 00:24:29.520
Funds made available by Congress have been
matched by state and local agencies and used

00:24:29.540 --> 00:24:30.880
to develop local health services.

00:24:31.800 --> 00:24:36.940
Under the Social Security Act, provisions
for this cooperative aid to these health services has been greatly extended.

00:24:39.620 --> 00:24:54.560
[Music.]

00:24:56.500 --> 00:25:00.480
The city health officer of a western city
receives a telephone call.

00:25:03.140 --> 00:25:05.980
He picks up the receiver and finds it is from
a local physician.

00:25:06.900 --> 00:25:11.300
This physician has a case the symptoms of
which resemble epidemic encephalitis, but

00:25:11.920 --> 00:25:14.360
there are some features which make this diagnosis
uncertain.

00:25:15.200 --> 00:25:19.659
The city health officer remarks that he is
greatly concerned, as he has had several similar

00:25:19.660 --> 00:25:21.520
cases recorded in the past few days.

00:25:29.780 --> 00:25:32.680
The city health officer decides to notify
the state health officer.

00:25:33.540 --> 00:25:36.260
He calls him by telephone and outlines the
local situation.

00:25:41.340 --> 00:25:45.500
The state health officer immediately reports
to the Surgeon General and asks him for aid.

00:26:01.140 --> 00:26:04.840
The city health officer calls an assistant
and instructs him to consult with the local

00:26:04.840 --> 00:26:06.700
physician; he is definitely alarmed.

00:26:09.300 --> 00:26:11.620
A little later a telegram is received from
the Surgeon General.

00:26:16.300 --> 00:26:20.000
After the Public Health Service officers have
conducted a preliminary investigation, they

00:26:20.000 --> 00:26:22.360
call a conference to discuss the situation.

00:26:26.440 --> 00:26:28.260
"Gentlemen this epidemic is growing.

00:26:29.380 --> 00:26:32.140
At least fifty new cases are being reported
daily.

00:26:33.420 --> 00:26:39.660
We must encourage close, harmonious cooperation
between ourselves, as representatives of the

00:26:39.660 --> 00:26:44.980
Public Health Service, and the city, county,
and state health authorities.

00:26:45.860 --> 00:26:51.160
The local medical schools have made available
their laboratories and other facilities."

00:26:52.160 --> 00:26:55.880
"What will be our policy as regards information
for the general public?"

00:26:57.020 --> 00:27:02.680
"The city health departments are notifying
the public frankly of the situation.

00:27:03.320 --> 00:27:05.560
Business must proceed as usual.

00:27:05.920 --> 00:27:06.860
There must be no panic."

00:27:08.400 --> 00:27:11.140
"There is an unusual plague of mosquitoes
just now.

00:27:12.080 --> 00:27:14.760
How long has that been connected to this outbreak?"

00:27:14.760 --> 00:27:17.280
"We’ll test that theory as fairly as possible."

00:27:19.780 --> 00:27:23.980
The mosquito tests were conducted on prison
inmates who voluntarily submitted themselves

00:27:23.980 --> 00:27:25.320
as laboratory animals.

00:27:25.680 --> 00:27:29.140
After these experiments were made, another
conference was called to discuss the results.

00:27:33.700 --> 00:27:36.420
"Dr. Williams, what are your results so far?"

00:27:37.400 --> 00:27:44.179
"The mosquito apparently does not transmit
this particular disease, however our investigations

00:27:44.180 --> 00:27:45.880
must be continued in other directions.

00:27:46.760 --> 00:27:51.240
The epidemic, despite all that has or has
not been done, is subsiding.

00:27:52.300 --> 00:27:56.680
We will transfer our studies to the National
Institute of Health in Washington."

00:27:58.160 --> 00:28:02.519
As result of intensive studies at the laboratory,
it was concluded that the disease was due

00:28:02.520 --> 00:28:07.920
to a virus, and several important new facts
regarding it were deduced from these investigations.

00:28:12.140 --> 00:28:17.360
In preventing diseases spread through unclean
milk, a safe milk supply is essential.

00:28:17.370 --> 00:28:20.559
Tuberculosis, (unintelligible) undulant fever,
typhoid fever,

00:28:20.560 --> 00:28:22.800
and other diseases are spread through contaminated
milk.

00:28:23.300 --> 00:28:27.820
The Public Health Service feels that clean
milk, properly pasteurized, is the only safe milk to drink,

00:28:28.300 --> 00:28:32.360
and it has conducted studies to determine
the efficiency of pasteurization procedures.

00:28:33.040 --> 00:28:37.680
These precautions assure a safe and clean
milk supply to the ultimate consumer, that

00:28:38.100 --> 00:28:42.840
is, if ultimate sanitary precautions are observed
by the ultimate consumers themselves.

00:28:43.860 --> 00:28:49.780
Another form of assistance to and cooperation
with the states is special aid in times of emergency.

00:28:49.920 --> 00:28:53.020
The disastrous floods which frequently occur
in the United States illustrate an emergency

00:28:53.020 --> 00:28:54.080
that may arise suddenly.

00:28:54.820 --> 00:28:58.660
During these floods, the states frequently
request the help of the sanitary engineers

00:28:58.669 --> 00:29:03.090
of the Public Health Service in providing
emergency purification and protection for

00:29:03.090 --> 00:29:06.260
town and city water supplies in the affected
areas.

00:29:10.980 --> 00:29:13.920
These requests for aid are met with prompt
response.

00:29:14.600 --> 00:29:18.660
In many instances, water purification machines
are quickly dispatched to the affected areas,

00:29:19.120 --> 00:29:21.740
and are put into operation by the sanitary
engineers.

00:29:27.340 --> 00:29:31.100
As the water is pumped into the reservoirs
or distributing systems,

00:29:31.100 --> 00:29:33.860
it is treated with chlorine to make it safe
for human consumption.

00:29:39.040 --> 00:29:45.500
[Music]

00:29:48.460 --> 00:29:50.880
In the
fight against disease from a public health standpoint,

00:29:51.020 --> 00:29:55.660
it is fundamentally important
to know when, where, in what numbers, and

00:29:55.660 --> 00:29:57.980
under what conditions various diseases are
occurring.

00:29:58.620 --> 00:30:01.740
The Public
Health Service records the important communicable

00:30:01.749 --> 00:30:04.140
diseases on charts which show their seasonal
prevalence.

00:30:04.629 --> 00:30:08.420
Note on these charts how closely
the cases for different years follow the same

00:30:08.420 --> 00:30:09.840
general seasonal patterns.

00:30:10.460 --> 00:30:14.220
Each separate line
across the chart represent a year for the particular disease.

00:30:17.300 --> 00:30:21.460
The Service maintains an intelligence office
regarding the occurrence of epidemic diseases

00:30:21.460 --> 00:30:26.360
in the United States and foreign countries,
and reports are received weekly from all American consuls.

00:30:26.920 --> 00:30:28.720
Their wide distribution is shown on the map.

00:30:30.380 --> 00:30:34.540
Whenever there's an outbreak of a quaratinable
disease anywhere in the world, the American

00:30:34.540 --> 00:30:37.520
consul at that place promptly cables this
information to Washington.

00:30:39.440 --> 00:30:41.720
Information is also obtained from many other
sources.

00:30:42.340 --> 00:30:47.560
From local health officers and state health
officers who report regularly by telegram,

00:30:48.020 --> 00:30:50.500
and on cards like the card shown here.

00:30:56.520 --> 00:31:00.340
Reports are also received from officers of
the Public Health Service stationed abroad.

00:31:00.980 --> 00:31:04.680
Health officers of foreign governments, and
international health organizations such as

00:31:05.160 --> 00:31:07.220
the International Office of Public Health,

00:31:07.680 --> 00:31:11.520
the Health Section of the League of Nations,
and the Pan American Sanitary Bureau.

00:31:12.760 --> 00:31:17.279
The information so collected is compiled and
published and is used by quarantine officers

00:31:17.280 --> 00:31:23.160
of the Public Health Service, by our own local
state health authorities, and by other governments

00:31:23.420 --> 00:31:24.180
throughout the world.

00:31:31.540 --> 00:31:45.400
[Music]

00:31:47.440 --> 00:31:52.040
Dr. L.S. Rowe, Director General of the Pan
American Union, addresses a recent conference:

00:31:54.320 --> 00:32:02.540
"Gentlemen of the conference: at this, your
closing session, I want to express to you,

00:32:03.560 --> 00:32:08.960
individually and collectively, the deep appreciation
of the Pan American Union for the privilege

00:32:09.700 --> 00:32:14.260
of having had you with us during the period
of your deliberations.

00:32:16.320 --> 00:32:22.560
It is no exaggeration to say that the Third
Pan American Conference of Directors of Health

00:32:23.640 --> 00:32:29.260
marks a distinct step forward in that struggle
of the nations of this continent

00:32:30.220 --> 00:32:37.160
to improve the conditions of life, to eliminate
the causes of disease, and to augment the

00:32:37.160 --> 00:32:40.120
efficiency of the masses of the people.

00:32:42.200 --> 00:32:48.600
I wish therefore to congratulate you, and
at the same to time assure you that in the

00:32:48.600 --> 00:32:57.480
future, as in the past, you may count on the
earnest and enthusiastic cooperation of everyone

00:32:57.480 --> 00:32:59.780
associated with the Pan American Union."

00:33:00.500 --> 00:33:04.860
Dr. H.S. Cumming, Director General of the Pan American
Sanitary Bureau now speaks:

00:33:05.440 --> 00:33:13.160
"Gentlemen, as Director of the Pan American
Sanitary Bureau and President of your conference,

00:33:13.160 --> 00:33:16.400
for which honor I thank you, I want to join
Dr. Rowe,

00:33:17.300 --> 00:33:23.220
in expressing our appreciation to you for
leaving your important administrative functions

00:33:23.230 --> 00:33:29.980
and to your respective governments for sending
you to this, the most successful sanitary

00:33:29.980 --> 00:33:31.160
conference we’ve had.

00:33:32.440 --> 00:33:41.000
A point of progress reported by you and your
countries, practical plans formulated, is

00:33:41.120 --> 00:33:43.500
by far the most successful conference we’ve
ever had.

00:33:43.500 --> 00:33:46.380
I wish you Godspeed back to your respective
homes."

00:33:49.360 --> 00:33:58.980
[[Music]

00:33:59.860 --> 00:34:04.020
Scientific studies dealing with the diseases
of man were made by the Public Health Service

00:34:04.020 --> 00:34:05.480
as early as 1886.

00:34:06.260 --> 00:34:10.660
These studies have gradually expanded until
today the research of the Public Health Service

00:34:10.670 --> 00:34:16.060
on the cause, method of spread, and means
of prevention of disease, is among the most

00:34:16.060 --> 00:34:17.880
important work that it performs.

00:34:22.030 --> 00:34:26.820
A research laboratory for the Public Health
Service called the Hygienic Laboratory, was

00:34:26.820 --> 00:34:28.240
established in 1901.

00:34:28.940 --> 00:34:32.560
In 1930, Congress changed its name to the
National Institute of Health.

00:34:36.280 --> 00:34:41.280
At this famous institute in Washington, D.C.,
most of the investigative work of the Public

00:34:41.280 --> 00:34:42.460
Health Service is conducted.

00:34:43.980 --> 00:34:47.360
The diseases and conditions studied by the
Service include a long list.

00:34:48.180 --> 00:34:50.100
Heart disease is public enemy number one.

00:34:50.740 --> 00:34:53.300
It is first on the list of causes of death.

00:34:53.300 --> 00:34:57.180
More than 300,000 persons die each year in
the United States from this cause.

00:34:57.180 --> 00:34:59.150
[Principal causes of death in the United States.

00:34:59.150 --> 00:35:00.150
Heart disease, cancer, apoplexy (cerebral
hemorage, etc.), nephritis (Brights Disease)]

00:35:00.150 --> 00:35:02.820
The electrocardiograph has aided greatly in
the study and diagnosis of heart disease.

00:35:04.780 --> 00:35:06.860
Next in importance to the cause of death is
cancer.

00:35:07.680 --> 00:35:12.200
This disease results in the death of about
135,000 people in the United States annually.

00:35:13.700 --> 00:35:17.780
Malaria is still an important public health
problem in at least 16 states of the Union.

00:35:18.180 --> 00:35:22.080
This mosquito born disease exacts a toll of
sickness of more the 2 million cases annually.

00:35:22.580 --> 00:35:24.560
This patient is having a malarial chill.

00:35:26.840 --> 00:35:29.640
The fight against malaria is the fight against
the malaria mosquito.

00:35:30.140 --> 00:35:34.300
The prevention of mosquito breeding by seeing
that no containers are left lying around to

00:35:34.300 --> 00:35:38.910
catch and hold water, and thus provide breeding
places for mosquitoes, and by eliminating

00:35:38.910 --> 00:35:41.520
all refuse piles, insofar as possible.

00:35:48.160 --> 00:35:52.640
In certain regions effective mosquito control
has been accomplished by dusting water areas

00:35:52.640 --> 00:35:53.620
with a poisonous mixture.

00:35:54.200 --> 00:35:55.680
This dusting is done from trucks,

00:35:58.600 --> 00:35:59.900
by hand dusting machine,

00:36:02.920 --> 00:36:05.560
and by airplanes according to the conditions
met with.

00:36:09.340 --> 00:36:13.780
Another effective method employed is the killing
of larvae, or wiggle tails, by the oiling

00:36:13.780 --> 00:36:14.560
of stagnant water.

00:36:15.340 --> 00:36:19.420
Other preventive measures include ditching
for draining and keeping mosquitoes out of

00:36:19.420 --> 00:36:20.940
the home by screening.

00:36:27.690 --> 00:36:31.460
The protection of the health of the industrial
worker has become a matter to which much attention

00:36:31.470 --> 00:36:32.540
has been given.

00:36:32.540 --> 00:36:37.140
New manufacturing processes have frequently
introduced new hazards to the health of workers.

00:36:37.320 --> 00:36:42.020
The control of occupational disease has come
within the province of the physician and the engineer.

00:36:42.960 --> 00:36:46.860
In many industries, dust has been found to
be a serious hazard to the health of the employees,

00:36:47.700 --> 00:36:51.930
and exhaustive studies of the various types
of dust in industry have been made by the

00:36:51.930 --> 00:36:52.800
Public Health Service.

00:36:56.400 --> 00:37:01.060
Dusts are collected at the plant and atmospheric
and other data are recorded.

00:37:03.520 --> 00:37:08.860
These dust samples are then taken to the laboratory,
where they are carefully examined to determine

00:37:08.870 --> 00:37:12.590
the concentration, the size distribution,

00:37:12.590 --> 00:37:14.800
and the chemical and other characteristics
of the particles.

00:37:18.960 --> 00:37:23.700
This young lady is seen making a dust count
from a sample that was taken at one of the plants.

00:37:31.360 --> 00:37:35.880
The Public Health Service has conducted studies
on the mottled enamel of teeth, a disfiguring

00:37:35.890 --> 00:37:40.220
condition caused by an excessive amount of
fluorine in the drinking water of certain

00:37:40.220 --> 00:37:41.550
areas of the United States.

00:37:42.160 --> 00:37:45.740
These studies have shown that mottled enamel
is more prevalent in this country than had

00:37:45.740 --> 00:37:46.280
been realized.

00:37:47.540 --> 00:37:51.480
The Public Health Service conducts studies
on stream pollution, a subject of growing

00:37:51.480 --> 00:37:55.240
importance with our constantly increasing
and concentrating population.

00:37:55.740 --> 00:38:00.660
New problems have arisen from the increase
of human waste discharge into streams but

00:38:00.660 --> 00:38:03.680
also from the increase and changing types
of industrial waste.

00:38:04.740 --> 00:38:10.820
[Public health aspects of venereal diseases]

00:38:12.160 --> 00:38:16.220
From a public health standpoint the venereal
diseases are one of the most important problems

00:38:16.220 --> 00:38:19.140
confronting those whose duty it is to conserve
the health of our nation.

00:38:19.900 --> 00:38:24.020
Special laboratories are devoted by the Public
Health Service to the study of various phases

00:38:24.020 --> 00:38:24.620
of this subject.

00:38:25.360 --> 00:38:29.880
One day simultaneous surveys of all sources
of treatment have been conducted by the Public

00:38:29.890 --> 00:38:34.520
Health Service in representative areas of
the United States covering approximately one

00:38:34.520 --> 00:38:36.480
fourth of the entire population of the country.

00:38:37.220 --> 00:38:41.720
Estimates derived from these surveys indicate
that more than a million and a half new cases

00:38:41.720 --> 00:38:44.280
of the venereal diseases seek treatment anually
in this country.

00:38:45.240 --> 00:38:49.440
Cooperative studies conducted by the Public
Health Service with five of the leading venereal

00:38:49.440 --> 00:38:53.280
disease clinics in this country indicate that
syphilis is largely curable.

00:38:53.860 --> 00:38:57.800
To obtain recovery however treatment must
be started within the first year of the disease.

00:38:58.680 --> 00:39:01.960
The Public Health Service cooperates with
state and local health departments in the

00:39:02.660 --> 00:39:05.700
development of campaigns directed against
the venereal diseases.

00:39:09.360 --> 00:39:19.640
[Background music playing]

00:39:21.060 --> 00:39:25.020
From time immemorial, the Law of the Sea has required vessels to provide

00:39:25.020 --> 00:39:26.660
medical attention for their seamen.

00:39:27.020 --> 00:39:30.580
This was a difficult matter for the owners
of ships in the early days of the republic.

00:39:31.080 --> 00:39:35.940
Therefore in order to encourage its struggling
merchant marines, Congress established the

00:39:35.940 --> 00:39:39.720
Marine Hospital Service in 1798 to relieve
the ships of this burden.

00:39:40.360 --> 00:39:44.660
The first Marine Hospital in Boston, which
was the first General Hospital in that city,

00:39:44.920 --> 00:39:50.620
furnished hospital care for sailors from some
of the famous war sloops and frigates of  the war of 1812.

00:39:58.380 --> 00:40:04.420
Today there are 25 modern, thoroughly equipped
hospitals in this service located within the United States.

00:40:07.980 --> 00:40:11.920
These hospitals have an aggregate bed capacity
of approximately 6,000 beds and give treatment

00:40:12.580 --> 00:40:18.420
to about 300,000 persons annually, while almost
as many more apply each year for other service

00:40:19.020 --> 00:40:20.420
including physical examination.

00:40:22.900 --> 00:40:27.380
New marine hospitals have recently been built
in Baltimore, Cleveland, Detroit, Galveston,

00:40:27.380 --> 00:40:31.620
Memphis, New Orleans, Norfolk, San Francisco,
and Seattle.

00:40:32.240 --> 00:40:36.770
The Marine Hospital at Stapleton, New York,
which is the one shown here, has been enlarged

00:40:36.770 --> 00:40:38.720
to make it a 1,000 bed institution.

00:40:41.120 --> 00:40:45.940
These hospitals are professionally staffed
by medical officers both competent and humane

00:40:46.340 --> 00:40:48.120
secured by examination and selection.

00:40:51.500 --> 00:40:56.800
Only qualified graduate nurses, professional
dietitians, and skilled therapeutic aides are employed.

00:40:59.300 --> 00:41:04.100
These hospitals have all the specialized services:
eye, ear, nose and throat;

00:41:04.820 --> 00:41:06.720
a thoroughly equipped x-ray department;

00:41:10.040 --> 00:41:12.220
dental department with the
most modern equipment

00:41:14.100 --> 00:41:16.080
hydrotherapy; physiotherapy;

00:41:16.400 --> 00:41:19.160
venereal disease; and some have a psychiatric
service.

00:41:19.840 --> 00:41:23.900
They are provided with the most modern appliances
for the diagnosis and treatment of disease.

00:41:28.440 --> 00:41:31.540
Dental treatment is furnished at all Marine
Hospitals by dental officers.

00:41:32.140 --> 00:41:37.020
Most of the patients entering, especially
the merchant seamen, are suffering from septic mouth conditions.

00:41:37.800 --> 00:41:41.880
With the elimination of dental infection,
many remarkable recoveries have been reported.

00:41:43.260 --> 00:41:46.840
The facilities of the marine hospitals are
available without cost to American seamen

00:41:46.840 --> 00:41:50.560
employed onboard any registered, enrolled,
or licensed vessel of the United States;

00:41:51.100 --> 00:41:53.480
to officers and enlisted men of the Coast
Guard;

00:41:56.780 --> 00:41:59.220
to officers and crews of vessels of the lighthouse
service;

00:42:00.540 --> 00:42:03.080
to certain keepers and assistant keepers of the lighthouses;

00:42:08.840 --> 00:42:11.140
to immigrants detained at the immigration
stations;

00:42:12.840 --> 00:42:15.580
to seamen from vessels belonging to the United States Army;

00:42:17.040 --> 00:42:20.000
to beneficiaries of the United States Employees
Compensation Commission;

00:42:22.160 --> 00:42:25.920
to members of the Civilian Conservation Corps
in various sections of the country;

00:42:28.260 --> 00:42:30.420
to patients of the United States Veterans
Administration;

00:42:32.660 --> 00:42:34.600
and to persons afflicted with leprosy.

00:42:34.700 --> 00:42:37.440
This is the National Leprosarium at Carville,
Louisiana.

00:42:38.200 --> 00:42:42.240
(unintelligible) for license as pilots, other
officers of vessels of United States registry,

00:42:42.240 --> 00:42:47.220
and lighthouse keepers, must pass an examination
conducted by medical officers of the Public Health Service.

00:42:47.800 --> 00:42:51.100
These examinations are for vision, for color
blindness, and for hearing.

00:42:51.700 --> 00:42:56.120
The service must also pass upon the physical
ability of sailors qualifying as able-bodied seamen.

00:42:58.260 --> 00:43:02.880
Regulations require all ships officers be
versed in first aid, therefore the Public

00:43:02.880 --> 00:43:07.360
Health Service has organized courses of instruction
for such candidates in a number of the  larger ports.

00:43:14.200 --> 00:43:18.820
Not only does the Service furnish medical
aid to the Coast Guard, but it also sends

00:43:18.830 --> 00:43:22.890
its medical officers with the cruising cutters
on the North Atlantic ice patrol to furnish

00:43:22.890 --> 00:43:25.260
medical care to the officers and crews of
these vessels.

00:43:26.120 --> 00:43:29.980
The Service also sends medical officers with
the Bering Sea's seal patrols.

00:43:35.860 --> 00:43:40.120
The Coast Guard makes an annual cruise along
the coast of Alaska.

00:43:40.120 --> 00:43:42.780
Medical and dental officers of the Service
are sent on this cruise.

00:43:43.420 --> 00:43:45.740
They give medical examinations and treatment
to the natives.

00:43:46.380 --> 00:43:48.480
These include dental treatment and extraction.

00:43:49.380 --> 00:43:53.560
This is the only medical service available
to many of these native Alaskans.

00:43:57.800 --> 00:44:02.780
The National Leprosarium, which is a Marine
Hospital at Carville, Louisiana, has under

00:44:02.780 --> 00:44:05.550
treatment more than 300 patients who are lepers.

00:44:05.550 --> 00:44:09.550
The Leprosarium has an administration building
and a main hospital.

00:44:09.550 --> 00:44:14.060
Treatment by the various methods and agents
used has yielded most encouraging results

00:44:14.060 --> 00:44:17.100
and there have been many recoveries or arrested
cases.

00:44:17.940 --> 00:44:22.320
During the last ten years, over 150 patients
have been discharged to their homes no longer

00:44:22.320 --> 00:44:25.060
a menace to the public health, and the leprosy
arrested.

00:44:27.300 --> 00:44:31.800
Sports are provided by baseball diamonds and
tennis courts, and the younger patients greatly

00:44:31.800 --> 00:44:34.180
enjoy these outdoor recreational activities.

00:44:35.560 --> 00:44:39.580
The cottages for the patients are comfortable
and are provided with ground for gardens in

00:44:40.080 --> 00:44:41.920
which many of the patients take much delight.

00:44:42.600 --> 00:44:46.220
Life for these unfortunate persons is made
as comfortable and as pleasant as possible.

00:44:47.400 --> 00:44:51.520
In the attractive inner court two leper children
may be seen playing around the pool.

00:44:55.220 --> 00:44:59.260
Medical aid to vessels without a physician
has been made possible by the development of radio.

00:45:00.340 --> 00:45:04.880
Frequently, men are injured or suddenly develop
an acute illness on board ships far out at sea.

00:45:06.120 --> 00:45:11.100
If there is no physician aboard, the Public
Health Service is notified by radio.

00:45:11.980 --> 00:45:15.480
Many lives are saved each year thanks to this
radio service.

00:45:16.720 --> 00:45:18.780
"[Hold Chatham] radio for medical advice."

00:45:18.780 --> 00:45:19.700
"Aye, aye, captain."

00:45:20.140 --> 00:45:31.980
[Morse code signals being sent]

00:45:32.780 --> 00:45:37.140
The message from the vessel is received by
a commercial radio station which immediately

00:45:37.140 --> 00:45:39.680
relays it by telephone to the nearest Marine
Hospital.

00:45:41.180 --> 00:45:44.340
"Seamen suffering from sore throat for two
days.

00:45:44.760 --> 00:45:46.640
Now has temperature 104.

00:45:46.880 --> 00:45:47.660
Slight cough.

00:45:47.800 --> 00:45:48.600
Face flushed.

00:45:48.620 --> 00:45:49.900
Appears seriously ill.

00:45:50.380 --> 00:45:51.680
Request medical advice.

00:45:52.180 --> 00:45:54.340
Signed, Master of SS Columbia."

00:45:54.660 --> 00:45:59.200
"Send this reply: man apparently has acute
tonsillitis.

00:46:01.120 --> 00:46:02.760
Put him to bed on liquid diet.

00:46:03.580 --> 00:46:05.440
Have him drink cold water freely.

00:46:06.020 --> 00:46:08.820
Use hot alkaline gargle every two hours.

00:46:09.500 --> 00:46:12.960
Give 10 grains of aspirin every three hours
for four doses.

00:46:13.580 --> 00:46:15.380
Report progress in 12 hours.

00:46:16.120 --> 00:46:18.020
Sign this, 'U.S. Marine Hospital'"

00:46:18.440 --> 00:46:19.240
"Very well sir."

00:46:22.280 --> 00:46:25.640
A merchant seaman may have been suddenly attacked
by illness on approaching port.

00:46:26.160 --> 00:46:29.640
Here again, the medical officers of the Marine
Hospital are notified by radio.

00:46:30.140 --> 00:46:33.760
But in this case an ambulance is sent from
the hospital to the dock to meet the boat.

00:46:34.720 --> 00:46:36.900
The patient is taken off the vessel on a stretcher.

00:46:38.800 --> 00:46:41.580
He is placed in the ambulance and rushed to
the Marine Hospital.

00:46:45.100 --> 00:46:49.920
On arriving at the hospital, he is taken directly
to the ward for examination and diagnosis.

00:46:52.320 --> 00:46:55.940
The medical officers examine him carefully,
and with the aid of the history of the case

00:46:55.940 --> 00:46:58.300
that is furnished them, they make their diagnosis.

00:46:58.300 --> 00:47:01.400
In this instance, it is definitely an acute
attack of appendicitis.

00:47:02.080 --> 00:47:03.930
The patient must be operated on at once.

00:47:04.260 --> 00:47:08.740
He is therefore taken to the operating room
where the troublesome appendix is removed.

00:47:17.040 --> 00:47:28.480
[background music playing]

00:47:28.490 --> 00:47:32.840
An act of Congress requires that the medical
care in federal penal and correctional institutions

00:47:32.840 --> 00:47:34.520
be furnished by the Public Health Service.

00:47:35.000 --> 00:47:41.980
The prisoners are given thorough physical
examinations: eye, ear, nose, and throat;

00:47:43.460 --> 00:47:47.760
chest; dental; and other examinations.

00:47:48.520 --> 00:47:50.900
They are also given various types of mental
tests.

00:47:50.900 --> 00:47:55.510
These mental tests will afford valuable data
for the study of different types and characteristics

00:47:55.510 --> 00:47:59.020
of prison inmates which differentiate delinquents
from non-delinquents.

00:48:02.990 --> 00:48:07.240
When the United States Public Health Service
Hospital was established in Lexington, Kentucky,

00:48:07.240 --> 00:48:11.070
the problem of narcotic drug addiction was
put under the banner of medicine.

00:48:11.070 --> 00:48:15.000
Until that time, this problem had been regarded
almost solely as a correctional one.

00:48:15.560 --> 00:48:20.280
The hospital, consisting of a group of buildings,
covers an area of approximately 12 acres.

00:48:24.660 --> 00:48:29.700
The buildings are constructed in quadrangular
form, providing a large central court serving

00:48:29.700 --> 00:48:33.060
as an entrance plaza to the various departments
and units of the hospital.

00:48:35.280 --> 00:48:39.620
From here one gains access to these units,
especially provided for the reception and

00:48:39.630 --> 00:48:41.110
treatment of new admissions,

00:48:41.110 --> 00:48:45.400
for the treatment of those suffering from
inter-current diseases, and for the intensive

00:48:45.400 --> 00:48:48.460
study of patients and to those requiring special
forms of treatment.

00:48:48.780 --> 00:48:52.080
This part of the institution constitutes the
professional center of the hospital.

00:48:53.600 --> 00:48:57.800
To meet the needs for a better treatment for
drug addiction, special studies of patients are necessary

00:48:58.600 --> 00:49:01.800
The hospital is fully equipped and adequately
staffed for this purpose.

00:49:06.860 --> 00:49:11.920
Opportunities for outdoor work are afforded
the patients through the operation of a thousand acre farm.

00:49:12.720 --> 00:49:15.680
These farm activities include the operation
of a modern dairy,

00:49:18.340 --> 00:49:19.380
the raising of hogs,

00:49:21.240 --> 00:49:21.980
and poultry,

00:49:23.840 --> 00:49:25.860
and intensive truck farming.

00:49:29.020 --> 00:49:31.860
Indoor work for patients includes the operation
of a laundry,

00:49:34.400 --> 00:49:38.940
a modern garment shop for the manufacture
of clothing worn by the patients not for sale,

00:49:39.240 --> 00:49:43.580
and other activities that are necessary for
the maintenance and operation of the hospital.

00:49:44.820 --> 00:49:49.300
Supervised outdoor recreation is desirable
and necessary for the health of the patients.

00:49:49.740 --> 00:49:52.760
It promotes good fellowship and normal human
relationships.

00:50:01.220 --> 00:50:06.320
The career officers of the Public Health Service
constitute a mobile sanitary corps whose members

00:50:06.320 --> 00:50:10.480
are available for service whenever needed
in the United States or foreign countries

00:50:11.100 --> 00:50:15.460
for epidemic duty, for quarantine duty, or
for investigation work.

00:50:20.080 --> 00:50:24.720
The honor roll contains the names of many
men and women who have contracted diseases

00:50:24.720 --> 00:50:28.460
in line of duty, and of many who have made
the supreme sacrifice.

00:50:29.560 --> 00:50:34.360
These workers conducted their investigations
fearlessly with full knowledge of the dangers

00:50:34.360 --> 00:50:35.770
that confronted them.

00:50:35.770 --> 00:50:40.880
They've dedicated themselves to humanity and
made their sacrifice on the altar of science.

00:50:43.520 --> 00:50:47.720
Other workers were not less fearless, but
more fortunate; not less assiduous in their

00:50:47.720 --> 00:50:50.600
devotion to duty, but more favored on the
field of battle.

00:50:51.720 --> 00:50:57.220
The Public Health Service conducts its relentless
fight against disease silently and steadily,

00:50:57.680 --> 00:51:01.840
no martial music to inspire, no tumult or
shouting to sustain.

00:51:02.620 --> 00:51:03.880
The battlefield is silent.

00:51:04.340 --> 00:51:09.700
But the grim fight, the personal danger, the
satisfaction of accomplishment are there,

00:51:10.380 --> 00:51:15.200
even though the fight is frequently directed
against an unseen and an unknown enemy.

00:51:16.200 --> 00:51:35.560
[Music]

